I propose that we set the following deadlines for voting on the
"Attitudinals and Discursives" checkpoint:

June 18: Digressives SEI SEhU TO TOI (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
June 25: Vocatives COI DOI DOhU (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
July 2: Evidentials UI2 (Shepherd: Arnt Johansen)
July 9: Discursives UI3 (Shepherd: Arnt Johansen)
July 16: Text Structure Discursives UI3a UI3c UI6 (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
July 23: Highlight Discursives UI3b (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
July 30: Intensifiers CAI (Shepherd: Theodore Reed)
August 6: Realis Attitudinals UI1realis (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
August 13: Irrealis Attitudinals UI1irrealis (Shepherd: Jorge Llambias)
August 20: Attitudinal Specifiers UI4 UI7 FUhE FUhO (Shepherd: Adam Lopresto)
August 27: Attitudinal Modifiers UI5 (Shepherd: Theodore Reed)

The last two are not complete, so leaving them for last will give the
shepherds more than two months to work on them. I think the rest are
all ready for voting. Probably there are some typos and minor details to
adjust, so it would be important that every BPFK member reads them,
comments if necessary, and votes.

If all goes well, we can be done with this checkpoint by the end of
August, with only a few years of delay. What do you all think?

